  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.TextMeshPro::TMPro.TextMeshProUGUI
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "Be strong, be faster, be best one. And do your homework every day. \nHere should be a lot of text but i don't know what definetly should do with you. So how is your day? I believe that everythink is fine. I will add some recipes of pancakes for u guys:\nPancake Ingredients\nYou likely already have everything you need to make this pancake recipe. If not, here's what to add to your grocery list:\n\n\xB7 Flour: This homemade pancake recipe starts with all-purpose flour.\n\xB7 Baking powder: Baking powder, a leavener, is the secret to fluffy pancakes.\n\xB7 Sugar: Just a tablespoon of white sugar is all you'll need for subtly sweet pancakes.\n\xB7 Salt: A pinch of salt will enhance the overall flavor without making your pancakes taste salty.\n\xB7 Milk and butter: Milk and butter add moisture and richness to the pancakes.\n\xB7 Egg: A whole egg lends even more moisture. Plus, it helps bind the pancake batter together.\n\nHow to Store and Reheat Pancakes\nStore leftover pancakes in an airtight container in the fridge for about a week. Refrain from adding toppings (such as syrup) until right before you serve them so the pancakes don't get soggy.\n\nTo reheat pancakes, you have a few options: warm a batch in a 350 degrees F oven (covered) for 8 to 10 minutes, microwave individual pancakes in 20 to 30 second bursts with a damp paper towel, or reheat them in a skillet over medium-low heat for 30\u201360 seconds per side until warmed through.\n\ncloseup of pancakes on a plate with syrup and butter\nDotdash Meredith Food Studios\nCan You Save Pancake Batter?\nDon't let leftover pancake batter go to waste! Store the batter in an airtight container in the fridge for up to two days. If you plan to keep it longer than that, it's best to freeze the batter.\n\nCan You Freeze Pancakes?\nYes, you can freeze pancakes and pancake batter.\n\n\xB7 To freeze cooked pancakes: Allow the pancakes to cool completely, then arrange them in a single layer on a baking sheet (make sure the edges aren't touching). Flash freeze for a few hours or up to overnight. Reheat in an oven set to 350 degrees F until warmed through.\n\xB7 To freeze pancake batter: Ladle the pancake batter in serving size portions into freezer bags, then wrap the bags in foil. Freeze flat for up to one month. Thaw in the refrigerator overnight.\n\nAllrecipes Community Tips and Praise\n\"This recipe is one to hand down to your grandkids,\" raves ashleyalbertine. \"Fluffy and delicious. Haven't bought a box of pancake mix in months! Just add a bit of vanilla and poof! Magic.\"\n\n\"Perfect,\" according to Laura W. \"Delicious! If you're looking for some thick, hearty pancakes these are the ones to make! Made them exactly as the recipe states and then added mini-chocolate chips to each cake as they were on the frying pan (before flipping).\"\n\n\"I made this recipe exactly as written...the kids were eating them off the plate faster than I could cook them,\" says aellis1970. \"They are so delicious, they were eaten without syrup.\"\n\nEditorial contributions by Corey Williams\n\n\nKeep Screen Awake\nIngredients\n\n1/2x\n\n1x\n\n2x\n\nOriginal recipe (1X) yields 8 servings\n\n1 \xBD cups all-purpose flour\n\n3 \xBD teaspoons baking powder\n\n1 tablespoon white sugar\n\n\xBC teaspoon salt, or more to taste\n\n1 \xBC cups milk\n\n3 tablespoons butter, melted\n\n1 large egg\n\nDirections\nGather all ingredients.\n\nIngredients for pancakes including flour milk an egg melted butter baking powder and salt in bowls\nAllrecipes / Qi Ai\nSift flour, baking powder, sugar, and salt together in a large bowl. Make a well in the center and add milk, melted butter, and egg; mix until smooth.\n\nWhisk in batter inside a glass mixing bowl\nAllrecipes / Qi Ai\nHeat a lightly oiled griddle or pan over medium-high heat. Pour or scoop the batter onto the griddle, using approximately 1/4 cup for each pancake; cook until bubbles form and the edges are dry, about 2 to 3 minutes.\n\nThree pancakes cooking in a skillet midway through preparation\nAllrecipes / Qi Ai\nFlip and cook until browned on the other side. Repeat with remaining batter.\n\nThree pancakes in a frying pan\nAllrecipes / Qi Ai\nServe and enjoy!\n\nPlate with pancakes topped with butter along with syrup and utensils at the side\nAllrecipes / Qi Ai\nFrom the Editor\nThe salt amount has been reduced based on review feedback. The original recipe called for 1 teaspoon.\n\nNutrition Facts (per serving)\n158\nCalories\n6g\nFat\n22g\nCarbs\n5g\nProtein\n\nShow Full Nutrition Label"
